.TH DEPLOYWEB 1 "@MAN_DATE@" "deployweb @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deployweb \- website deployment utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deployweb
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPROJECT-DIR\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBdeployweb\fR is a utility for deploying websites to remote servers. It finds
the project root (by looking for package.json), builds the project using pnpm,
syncs the dist/ directory to the server, and configures Apache virtual hosts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fINAME\fR
Select profile name or config file path. If not specified, deployweb tries to
auto-select a profile from \fI~/.config/deployweb/\fR using the project name.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-ssh-host\fR \fIHOST\fR
SSH host used for file sync and remote commands. Accepts \fIhost\fR or
\fIhost:port\fR.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-ssh-port\fR \fIPORT\fR
SSH port (default: 22).
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-ssh-user\fR \fIUSER\fR
SSH user.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-ssh-identity\fR \fIFILE\fR
SSH identity file.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-ssh-visual-host-key\fR
Enable SSH visual host key output.
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-ssh-sudo-pw\fR \fIPW\fR
Sudo password for remote commands; uses \fBsudo -A\fR.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-server\fR \fI[protocol://]HOST[:PORT]\fR
Add Apache virtual-host binding. May be used multiple times. Protocol defaults
to HTTP when omitted.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-www-root\fR \fIDIR\fR
Remote web root directory (default: \fI/var/www\fR).
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-www-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
Deploy directory relative to \fB\-\-www-root\fR (default: project name).
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-conf-name\fR \fINAME\fR
Apache config/site name (default: basename of \fB\-\-www-dir\fR).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-priority\fR \fINUM\fR
Reserved priority option.
.TP
\fB\-O\fR, \fB\-\-apache-options\fR \fIOPTS\fR
Apache \fB<Directory>\fR options string.
.TP
\fB\-B\fR, \fB\-\-always\fR
Always run \fBpnpm build\fR before deployment.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-sync-only\fR
Sync files only; skip Apache configuration.
.TP
\fB\-\-dryrun\fR
Dry run mode. Print actions without executing remote changes.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Reduce verbosity.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase verbosity.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Display help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration files are stored in \fI~/.config/deployweb/\fR. Each profile
is a text file with the following format:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ssh-host: <host>
ssh-port: <port>
user: <ssh username>
identity-file: <keyfile>
visual-host-key: yes/no
sudo-pw: <password>
server: [protocol://]host[:port]
www-root: <path>
www-dir: <path>
conf-name: <name>
apache-options: <apache directory options>
.fi
.RE
.PP
The configuration options are:
.TP
\fIssh-host\fR
SSH target host used for rsync/remote commands.
.TP
\fIssh-port\fR (optional)
SSH port. Defaults to 22.
.TP
\fIserver\fR
Apache virtual host binding in \fI[protocol://]host[:port]\fR form.
.TP
\fIwww-root\fR
Base directory on the server where websites are deployed.
.TP
\fIwww-dir\fR
Deploy directory under \fIwww-root\fR.
.TP
\fIuser\fR (optional)
SSH username for connecting to the server.
.TP
\fIidentity-file\fR (optional)
Path to SSH private key file.
.TP
\fIvisual-host-key\fR (optional)
Set to "yes" or "no" to control SSH host key verification
(StrictHostKeyChecking).
.TP
\fIsudo-pw\fR (optional)
Sudo password for remote commands. When specified, uses \fBsudo -A\fR
with an askpass script that reads from \fILC_SUDO_PW\fR environment
variable.
.TP
\fIconf-name\fR (optional)
Apache config/site name.
.TP
\fIapache-options\fR (optional)
Apache Directory options. Defaults to "\fB+Indexes +MultiViews +FollowSymLinks\fR" if
not specified.
.SH WORKFLOW
The deployment process follows these steps:
.IP 1. 4
Find project root by searching for package.json starting from PROJECT-DIR
.IP 2. 4
Build the project using \fBpnpm build\fR
.IP 3. 4
Rsync the \fIdist/\fR directory to \fI<www-root>/<www-dir>\fR
.IP 4. 4
Generate and install Apache virtual host configuration from \fIserver\fR entries
.IP 5. 4
Enable the site and reload Apache
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Deploy to default profile:
.B deployweb /path/to/project
.TP
Deploy with specific profile and server binding:
.B deployweb -c production -n example.com /path/to/project
.TP
Deploy with mixed HTTP and HTTPS bindings:
.B deployweb -n example.com -n https://www.example.com:443 /path/to/project
.TP
Deploy with custom remote root and sync only:
.B deployweb -r /srv/www -d app/current -s /path/to/project
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/deployweb/\fR
Directory containing profile configuration files.
